menu "RadioFoundry Gateway SDR (sdr)"

    config RDOF_FEATURE_SDR
        bool "SDR receive path"
        default y
        help
            The channelizer, FM discriminator, DMR burst demod and AFC (the SDR
            receiver). Off, the component builds empty.

    config RDOF_FEATURE_SDR_AGC
        bool "Front-end gain control law"
        default y
        depends on RDOF_FEATURE_SDR
        help
            Turn the tuner gain down while samples clip, back up slowly.

    config RDOF_FEATURE_SDR_BUILTIN_FFT
        bool "Built-in FFT"
        default y
        depends on RDOF_FEATURE_SDR
        help
            The portable mixed-radix FFT. Turn it off when the firmware supplies
            rdof_fft_new / rdof_fft_run / rdof_fft_free itself (for example on esp-dsp).

    config RDOF_FEATURE_SDR_RECEIVER
        bool "Multi-channel receiver with call trackers"
        default y
        depends on RDOF_FEATURE_SDR && RDOF_FEATURE_TRACKER
        help
            One tuner's channels, each with a demod and a call tracker,
            and AFC fed back to the channelizer.

    config RDOF_SDR_DSP_IRAM
        bool "The receive path's hot code in internal RAM (IRAM)"
        default n
        depends on RDOF_FEATURE_SDR
        help
            demod, fm, channelizer, fft and receiver (and the firmware's esp-dsp glue) run from IRAM instead of
            through the 16 KB flash instruction cache both cores share. About 33 KB of internal RAM, which the
            DSP buffers then don't get (more of them go to PSRAM). An experiment: compare the self-test's
            "prof" lines with and without (sdkconfig.defaults.dspfast).

endmenu
